---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — 3G Intelligence" description="" lang="en">
  <div class="legal-doc">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="date">Last updated: October 2026</div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>3G Intelligence is an artificial intelligence consultancy offering diagnostics and automation solutions for businesses. Contact: <a href="mailto:gonzalo@3gi.cl">gonzalo@3gi.cl</a></p>

    <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Phone number when contacting via WhatsApp</li>
      <li>Messages sent to the WhatsApp bot</li>
      <li>Business information entered in the Test ERA form (name, sector, size, processes)</li>
      <li>Traffic analytics cookies (Google Analytics and PostHog) and advertising measurement cookies (LinkedIn) — see section 8</li>
      <li>A record of the steps of your journey in the ERA Test (page and step reached and, only if you accept cookies, campaign parameters) — see section 8</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To qualify and process Test ERA report requests</li>
      <li>To follow up commercially with the prospect</li>
      <li>To generate internal diagnostic reports</li>
      <li>To analyze and improve the ERA Test journey and measure the results of our campaigns</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or transfer data to third parties. We use the following service providers under their own privacy policies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — natural language processing (Claude AI)</li>
      <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> — embeddings generation for semantic search</li>
      <li><strong>Meta</strong> — WhatsApp Business messaging channel</li>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — data storage</li>
      <li><strong>Hetzner</strong> — infrastructure hosting</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — website traffic analytics (Google Analytics), only if you accept analytics cookies (see section 8)</li>
      <li><strong>PostHog</strong> — product analytics and recordings of the journey on the site, only if you accept cookies (see section 8)</li>
      <li><strong>LinkedIn</strong> — advertising conversion measurement (LinkedIn Insight Tag), only if you accept cookies (see section 8)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These providers are located in the United States. The transfer is supported by the Standard Contractual Clauses approved by Chile's Ministry of Economy.</p>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Data is retained for the duration of the business relationship or until the user requests deletion.</p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You may request access, correction, deletion, objection, and portability of your data at any time. You also have the right not to be subject to decisions based solely on automated processing of your data that significantly affect you, to request an explanation of such decisions, and to request human intervention or review. Write to us at <a href="mailto:gonzalo@3gi.cl">gonzalo@3gi.cl</a>.</p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>Data is stored on secure servers with restricted access. No passwords or financial information are shared through our channels.</p>

    <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
    <p>With your consent we use three third-party tools: Google Analytics (via Google Tag Manager) to understand how this site is used; PostHog to analyze the ERA Test journey (page views, clicks, completed steps and recordings of your browsing on the site); and, if you arrive from a LinkedIn ad, the LinkedIn Insight Tag to measure how many people complete the ERA Test after seeing the ad. They are only loaded if you accept them in the notice shown on your first visit: if you reject them, none of them is loaded.</p>
    <p>Even if you reject cookies, the ERA Test and the resources pages record the steps of your journey (for example, which test question you are on and the page) using a random identifier that exists only in the memory of the page: it is not stored in your browser, it is lost when you change page or close it, and no campaign parameters are recorded. With your consent, that identifier is stored in your browser while the tab stays open, and the campaign parameters of the address you visited (for example, which ad you came from) are also recorded, so we can follow your full journey. In both cases the record does not include your name, email or company data, and it is stored only on our own servers (Supabase). We also count, without identifying you, how many people accept or reject cookies. We use it to learn where people drop out of the test and improve it.</p>
    <p>You can change your cookie decision at any time via the "Cookie preferences" link at the bottom of this page.</p>
    <table class="cookie-table">
      <tr class="row-head">
        <th>Cookie</th>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Duration</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>_ga</td>
        <td>Google</td>
        <td>Distinguish users (analytics)</td>
        <td>2 years</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>_ga_*</td>
        <td>Google</td>
        <td>Maintain session state (analytics)</td>
        <td>2 years</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>tgi_consent (localStorage)</td>
        <td>3G Intelligence</td>
        <td>Remember your consent decision</td>
        <td>Until you delete it</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>bcookie, lidc, UserMatchHistory (and similar)</td>
        <td>LinkedIn</td>
        <td>Measure advertising conversions</td>
        <td>Per LinkedIn's cookie policy</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>ph_*_posthog (cookie and localStorage)</td>
        <td>PostHog</td>
        <td>Distinguish visitors and sessions (analytics and recordings)</td>
        <td>1 year</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>_3gi_fsid, _3gi_futm (sessionStorage, only if you accept)</td>
        <td>3G Intelligence</td>
        <td>Follow your full journey in the ERA Test and which campaign you came from</td>
        <td>Until you close the tab</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-doc {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    padding: 140px 24px 48px;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-doc h1 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #00E891;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legal-doc .date {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #6B7280;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .legal-doc h2 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #EEF1F6;
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }
  .legal-doc p, .legal-doc li {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #9CA3AF;
  }
  .legal-doc ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .legal-doc li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .legal-doc a { color: #00E891; text-decoration: none; }
  .cookie-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .cookie-table th, .cookie-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 10px;
    border-right: 1px solid #1F2937;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1F2937;
  }
  .cookie-table th:last-child, .cookie-table td:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .cookie-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .cookie-table .row-head {
    background: rgba(0,232,145,0.1);
  }
  .cookie-table th { color: #EEF1F6; }
  .cookie-table td { color: #9CA3AF; }
</style>
